    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §64-l, Town L; add Art 31-J §§1450-a - 1450-o, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6664\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the town law, in relation to authorizing the town of\nCopake to establish community preservation funds; to amend the tax law,\nin relation to authorizing the town of Copake to impose a real estate\ntransfer tax with revenues therefrom to be deposited in said community\npreservation fund; and providing for the repeal of certain provisions of\nthe tax law upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the. Town of Copake, in Columbia County, to establish a\ncommunity preservation fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the Town Law by adding a new Section 64-1 establishing\nTown of Copake preservation funds.\n\n§ 2: Amends the Town Law by adding a new Article 314\n\n§ 3: Severability.\n\n§ 4: Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will give the Town of Copake, in Columbia County, the authori-\nty to create Community Preservation Funds to protect its farmland and\nopen space. This legislation has been requested by the Town of Copake.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that section\ntwo of this act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall\nhave become a law and shall expire December 31, 2045 when upon such date\nthe provisions of such section shall be deemed repealed.\n",
